---
import { SITE } from '@/config';
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro';
const updated = 'October 2026';
---
<Page
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data, which cookies are set, and how to opt out of personalised advertising.`}
  path="/privacy"
  lede={`Last updated ${updated}.`}
>
  <aside class="callout warn">
    <div class="eyebrow">Before you publish</div>
    <p>
      Replace <strong>[LEGAL ENTITY NAME]</strong> and <strong>[REGISTERED ADDRESS]</strong> below
      with your real details, and have this reviewed if you operate at scale. India's Digital
      Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 applies to you. This template is a starting point, not
      legal advice.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <p>
    This policy explains what {SITE.name} ("we") collects when you visit {SITE.domain}, why, and
    what you can do about it. The site is operated by <strong>[LEGAL ENTITY NAME]</strong>,
    <strong>[REGISTERED ADDRESS]</strong>, India.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We do not ask you to create an account and we do not collect your name, bank details, account
    numbers or credit report. Do not send us any of those.
  </p>
  <p>Collected automatically when you visit:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Standard server and analytics data: pages viewed, approximate location at city level, referring site, device and browser type, and time of visit.</li>
    <li>Cookies and similar identifiers set by third parties listed below.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you email us or use the contact form, we hold what you send us for as long as it takes to
    answer, and then delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site shows advertising. Google, as a third-party vendor, uses cookies to serve ads on this
    site. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on
    your visit to this and other sites.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You can opt out of personalised advertising at
      <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can opt out of other third-party vendors' cookies at
      <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google's own terms are in the
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Privacy &amp; Terms</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Third-party ad networks may also place cookies. We do not control those cookies and cannot
    switch them off on your behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics to understand which pages are useful. It sets cookies and records the
    data listed above. IP addresses are anonymised. You can block it with the
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    Some outbound links are affiliate links. Following one may let the destination set a cookie that
    tells them we referred you. We receive a commission on some products; we do not receive your
    personal data from them. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you may ask what personal data we hold
    about you, ask us to correct or erase it, and withdraw consent. Because we hold almost nothing,
    most requests are answered quickly. Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are in the EEA or UK, the GDPR gives you equivalent rights, including the right to
    complain to your local supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed at children under 18 and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Material changes to this policy will be noted here with a new "last updated" date.
  </p>
</Page>
